    {
      "id": "claim_6a62855ebdb6447eb072ea6a1c27cb35",
      "statement": "EVE sensitivity is driven by duration assumptions: net asset dollar duration slightly exceeds liability dollar duration (about $1,369mm per 100 bp), so EVE falls when rates rise; the Annual Report attributes this to fixed-rate mortgages and securities having longer duration than modeled deposits, and Pillar 3 assigns behavioral durations of 3.5 years to noninterest-bearing and 2.8 years to consumer interest-bearing deposits.",
